# Local development connection strings — Postgres 16 via `docker compose up -d
# postgres` (docker-compose.yml). Neon is used for CI and Vercel production;
# nothing here is read there.
#
# Copy to `.env` (gitignored — never commit real values) and fill in
# passwords of your choosing. architecture.md Part I §2.2: three roles, three
# connection strings, never consolidated — see packages/db/pool.ts.
#
# Each password below is used TWICE and must match in both places:
#   1. here, embedded in the *_DATABASE_URL that psql/drizzle-kit connect with
#   2. as the bare *_PW value, which `make migrate` passes to
#      packages/db/policies/001_roles_and_grants.sql to create/alter the role
# The two are independent env vars — this file does not expand one into the
# other — so if you change a password, update both lines.

# --- role passwords ---------------------------------------------------------

APP_USER_PW=changeme-app-user
CORPUS_WRITER_PW=changeme-corpus-writer
ANALYTICS_PW=changeme-analytics

# --- connection strings ------------------------------------------------------
# host/port/db match docker-compose.yml's `postgres` service. Role names are
# fixed by architecture.md §2.2 and packages/db/policies/001_roles_and_grants.sql.

# app_user — web app + every job EXCEPT corpus.record. Also the database
# superuser locally (docker-compose.yml sets POSTGRES_USER=app_user), so it is
# the connection `make migrate` uses to run `drizzle-kit migrate` and then
# (re-)create the other two roles.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://app_user:changeme-app-user@localhost:5432/compliance_data_layer

# corpus_writer — corpus.record ONLY, created by `make migrate` on first run.
CORPUS_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://corpus_writer:changeme-corpus-writer@localhost:5432/compliance_data_layer

# readonly_analytics — SELECT on corpus only, created by `make migrate` on first run.
ANALYTICS_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://readonly_analytics:changeme-analytics@localhost:5432/compliance_data_layer
